Z||000009||87FieroGTx||07-04-2001||04:27 AM|||| A lot of the SPEED parts like K&N air filters and bored out Throttle bodies take a lot of torque away but give you a little Horse Power so your faster on the top end but your bottom end suffers.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mblackwell||07-04-2001||08:01 AM||||I fishtailed exactly twice.  Once I ended up in the ditch, now I have a hump in the floor under the driver's seat.  The other time I went down an embankment and had to floor alternating forward and reverse to drive through some woods to get back on the road.  I both times were totally unintensional.  And no, I wasnt speeding.<P>Should I be able to spin the tires with my automatic v6 just by flooring it in drive? All it does is a tiny chirp, or nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000011||p4n1c||07-04-2001||08:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>I fishtailed a bit tonight, tried to hold it, but chickened out and hit the brakes and stopped before I went into a ditch.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>*cough*<P>Do you have an attraction to ditches by any chance?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Front-wheel drive, fishtailing and brakes don't mix.  I learned that the hard way on a gravel road, I ended up sideways sliding down a hill.  Turn where you want to go and give it some gas, that's always got me out of one.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4<BR>*Under Restoration*||||reg||10
Z||000012||Formula||07-04-2001||08:55 AM||||my auto doesnt chirp them off the line at all, it sometimes chirps second but thats it.. also peole tel me that I spin the tires but I can never ear it because the engine is so loud<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||firstfiero||07-04-2001||10:20 AM||||      I usually do it as I'm makeing the right turn out of work. When I first got the car I had to learn when racing to get the wheels rolling a bit for I stumped on it! If I didn't I would fish tail right through the intersection! Lose the whole shot and you lose the race. <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000014||RiceCooker||07-04-2001||02:40 PM||||So much of it depends on tires and even shocks too.<P>With my old tires, i could swim sideways at the lights a bit whenever i wanted but since i got my Pirelli P7000 225/40's it's tough to get more than a chirp, unless it's wet.<P>If it's raining, there's this little 4 way stop interesction right down my street. I stop and before making my left turn i rev it and dump the clutch. I go around the corner sideways using my throttle to steer, just like the ol dodge Viper. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> And it is a good stress reliever. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||The Dealer||07-04-2001||05:36 PM||||I haven't done any fish tailing with my Fiero, but I have a few experiences in other vehicles.  First off, I had a 1983 Chevette at one time, winter was the best, get it going down the street, yank the e-brake and pull the steering wheel hard, you could get two or three 360's almost everytime....lol<P>I put my Sonoma in the ditch once, out in the snow, fish tailing on the back roads... came around a corner too fast and in I went.....lol<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000016||ElricSI||07-04-2001||08:01 PM||||Me!<P>I love it when the road is wet.  I usually do it at highway entrances, no parked cars in case I lose it.  Wet road + turn + too much gas = fun fun fun.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Proud Owner of 85 GT||||reg||3
Z||000017||fiero56||07-04-2001||11:13 PM||||I was front seat passenger in a friends Celica today. We were changing lanes(60mph, exit ramp), the back-end started fish-tailing, he wasn't able to catch it(kept over-correcting), and the next thing I new we slammed into a concrete barrier 3 times. Damn glad I had my seatbelt on. That car is f'ed up bad. Dumped all the oil, blew the radiator, ATF was coming out, so was fuel, and we broke the one cement block divider. Looking at the car from passenger side where I was(all the major damage was on my side, we hit the wall three times as we spun), the car is literally about 3 feet shorter than before. Luckily, we never flipped(a damn SUV would most certainly have rolled), and we both got out unhurt, although his shoulder belt hurt his shoulder, he plan to see the doctor tommorrow, it didn't hurt at the time of the crash.<P>Be careful out there, my '86SE has a tendency to oversteer too, but I watch for and plan for it.||||reg||1
Z||000018||chester||07-05-2001||07:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RiceCooker:<BR><B>So much of it depends on tires and even shocks too.<P>With my old tires, i could swim sideways at the lights a bit whenever i wanted but since i got my Pirelli P7000 225/40's it's tough to get more than a chirp, unless it's wet.<P>If it's raining, there's this little 4 way stop interesction right down my street. I stop and before making my left turn i rev it and dump the clutch. I go around the corner sideways using my throttle to steer, just like the ol dodge Viper.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> And it is a good stress reliever. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have to agree that it really depends on the tire combo your running.  I used to have some BFGoodrich Euro T/A's on my GT (Which were off of the wifes GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) and I could lay a 50' patch of rubber with those. Found that out leaving Uhaul one day when they told me my reserved truck wasn't available  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">! Now I have some Dunlop SP9000's and they hook up like crazy glue.  They will literally skip on the ground 2 or 3 times and hookup.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Leadfoot||07-05-2001||10:11 AM||||My favorite manuver is the 180 fish tail.  I use it when I know I am gonna have to make a U-ee.  I had a friend in the car when I did it once.  He nearly crapped his shorts!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||BBBAD GT||07-05-2001||10:43 AM||||How about fishtailing at 50 mph?  I can do that with the Stang.....gotta love stupid power.<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000021||stsmithgt||07-05-2001||10:44 AM||||I caught a woppper of a fishtail the other day on my favorite off ramp that swings back over the highway.  I guess I should have slowed down below 100 when I passed that 25m.p.h. speed limit sign. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I was still on the brakes pretty hard by the time I got started into the curve. oops.  The back end came shooting out till I was almost looking out my side window. WAHOOOOO!!! Well, it was more like WHOA!...then WAHOOOO!  Luckily I got off the brakes and onto the gas fast enough, which hooked the tires right up and away I went.  I thought I was going to loose it for a moment because I whipped it into the corner so harshly.  It made it a lot more fun being able to power it through the curve then to spin out. WHAT A RUSH! That'll wake you up at 6:00 in the morning!<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000022||ChadMan||07-05-2001||11:05 AM||||Holy crap, fiero56!  I'm thanking the motorgods you're not dead - and that the destroyed car was only a Celica.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Burnouts are fun, but I don't do 'em often - Fiero clutches are too damned delicate and expensive for that.<P>The '84 would do some mean burnouts though.  <BR>Good running Duke + 185/80 tires + 4.10...run it up to 3500 & pop the clutch and it would light 'em up pretty good!<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||fiero56||07-05-2001||07:04 PM||||Yup, glad I'm here still too. He got a call from his insurance agent today. The car is totaled(duh). We hit hard enough that the engine was crushed, cracking the block, which caused the oil and ATF spill. The frame in front is so mangled it is irrepairable, and the rear sustained moderate frame damage. <P>Roads were "patchy-wet" as it had finished raining about 30 minutes prior. I'm just glad there was nobody around to hit us as we spun. It is unbelievable to me, but I was able to push the car off the highway as my buddy steered, even after it had sustained that much damage. He's going car shopping this weekend.<P>My '88 is impossible to get oversteer just by switching directions, I try.||||reg||1
Z||000024||AusFiero||07-06-2001||03:13 AM||||Myself and a friend had a great time once in a huge carpark after a flood had been through. The whole carpark was covered in river sand and burnouts, fist tailing or anything you wanted to do was in slow motion. Was quite fun at 18. And no it wasn't a Fiero getting sandblasted in the process, just an old Mazda that had one of them noisy little rotary things in it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000025||85seNUT||07-06-2001||12:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B><P>Roads were "patchy-wet" as it had finished raining about 30 minutes prior. I'm just glad there was nobody around to hit us as we spun. It is unbelievable to me, but I was able to push the car off the highway as my buddy steered, even after it had sustained that much damage. He's going car shopping this weekend.<P>My '88 is impossible to get oversteer just by switching directions, I try.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You had to push while he steered?  Dang he crashed, not you.  Seems to me like he should have pushed and steered for driving so wreakless, hes lucky to have a nice friend like you.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Seanh||07-06-2001||05:01 PM||||I have a heck of a time looseing traction with my automatic GT on dry pavement. Now after it rains, thats a whole 'nother story. I love my Fiero in the rain. Its the funnest damn thing on the road. I go out in that thing every time it rains. Dirt is fun too, but I can get the car to hook up alot easier when I want to in rain then on dirt. I don't like dirt tracks anymore, I have nightmares about them now even. I think Brandon can attest to my love for rain however. After it rains here, there is usally a huge puddle of water, about a foot deep in our mall parking lot. I haven't had a chance to take the Fiero thru there with some speed yet, since the "red-headed step child" took car of my front end, but I'm definatly looking forward to doing it once the car is done, again. <P>Then we got Brandon here, who enjoys doing his front wheel drive Grand Prix burnouts in rain...Damn off-dudy police officers spoil all the fun....I can only imagin what your going to do with a 3800 Fiero. I would suggest water-proof seat covers before you take Chris or Steve in that car....||||reg||1
Z||000027||MooCow||07-06-2001||06:46 PM||||Man I have never fishtailed cause I am to affraid of hurting my car.  I garentee I can do since I have a 3.4 with 4:10 gears.  I just don't want to take a chance and ruin something.  I baby this car far to much.<BR>Someone needs to show me what my car can really do.<BR>                              Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
Z||000028||mrgone||07-07-2001||12:48 AM||||well, i learned what a v6 could do this week, actually in my parents family car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>so i was pulling out of my friends driveway to do my usual burnout i used to do with moms 97 escort (may it rest in peices) only this time i had dads 93 acclaim, 3.0 v6 <P>came out of a driveway in reverse, gave it some gas, slapped into drive and i floored it. engine roared and the tires lit up. tires spun hard for about 20-30 feet with it floored, then i started to feather the gas. i was surprised the tires still spun hard. and after about 6 car lengths, tires still spinning i hit the brakes. only because i was like :O  went back to the scene and, man. that was a wicked strip. sure beat the 6 footers the escort could do.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000029||firstfiero||07-07-2001||10:47 AM||||       The friend that sold me the car babyed it all the time. Never drov it fast one time!! What the hell is the point of haveing the v6 if your not going to drive her the way the car gods intended. I don't beat my car non stop. But I sure don't have a problem with haveing some fun now and then!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000030||Seanh||07-07-2001||11:36 AM||||No kidding, if you like putting around everywhere, get a METRO. I love rear wheel drive w/FWD transaxle, really makes for some awesome burnouts.<P>On another note, I managed to get my 81 4 banger Porsche 924, 5 spd, to do a 36 ft. burnout in the parking lot. I was a little pissed that day, but I didn't really mean to light 'em up for 36 ft, just looking for a noticable tire squeal that they could hear inside. And let me tell ya, this car is a beater from the word go. No hood, broken windshield, *custom* window chalk paint job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, bumper keeps falling off too.||||reg||1
Z||000031||firstfiero||07-07-2001||01:44 PM||||     I had a 77 Porsche 924. I loved that little car. I bought it with a blown enging. My dad and I found an engine and did the swap. The drive home from my parents house with it still stands as the greatest ride I ever had for 2 reasons....1) At that time in my life and as a child all I ever wanted was a Porsche...any Porsche!!  2) It was the biggest task I ever took on and acomplished! Still is! Their quirky little cars with electric bugs and all but you don't see many of them around!! <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000032||Seanh||07-07-2001||02:52 PM||||I bought mine for $100 about 2 months ago. The hood had come up while driving at 60 mph, bent the hood and broke the windshield, so he was just going to junk the car and I told him I'd give him $100 for it, and he told me to pick it up the next day. All and all, its gotten me in some trouble, but its sooooo much fun. Its really embarrasing to be seen in right now, but its definaly a party car. I'm thinking of fixing it up, painting it yellow or red w/black racing strips down the middle. Get a black interior with some descent seats, and redo the rest myself. Keep the resto fairly cheap and then when my "red-headed step child" (not MY child, but a step child still) wants to autocross one of my cars they wouldn't total the Fiero, again. Maybe rebuild the engine, not sure how many miles it has on it as the OD quit 5 years ago at 82K. It definatly needs a new clutch, its horrible but drivable right now. <P>What engine did you swap into it? Or did you rebuild the stock one? I am wanting to put a damn bigger enging in there, but apperently none of the new Porsche engines are compatable. And if I can't find a drop  in, with little to no modification, I might just as well drop a 350 in it, its been done. Parhaps Archie could help me with that one....||||reg||1
Z||000033||firstfiero||07-07-2001||03:54 PM||||    bought mine for 750 bucks and then found an engine in ohio for 500. Had to buy a new alternator and some other odds and ends costing me about 400. The worst thing about the car was buying parts if you couldn't find them at a junkyard...which was damn hard to do...you had to pay some hefty prices. I paid 250 for a rebuilt windshield wiper motore!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  It was going to cost me 2 grand just for parts to rebuild if I wouldn't have found another engine.  <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000034||fiero56||07-08-2001||12:38 AM||||<B>firstfiero</B>:<P>You bought that engine from that wrecked Formula John Altman had didn't you? Had like 60K miles on it at the time. <P>I'm still pissed about that...not your fault, previous "buyer" backed out...||||reg||1
Z||000035||JohnAC||07-08-2001||12:46 AM||||My best bud, Dale, had a '83 Firebird w/ the stock 2.8 in it.  He had just gotten it a few weeks earlier and we were out playing.  He took me to some large dirt parking lot to do donuts.  I'm like, WTF are we in dirt?  Near where we live there is a 2-lane highway w/ crossroads that are awesome for U-turns.  So I got him into my Fiero early morning (3am).  Was doin bout 85 down the highway, cut the wheel and let off the gas fishtailed through the opening in the median then slammed on the gas and regained going in opposite direction.  He tried to do it w/ his Firebird the week after and hit the median, luckily he only bent a rim and blew a tire.||||reg||12
Z||000036||firstfiero||07-08-2001||11:02 AM||||      Don't know where it came from. A local import junkyard tracked it down. Like I said right as I was getting ready to give up I got a call and had it. This was about 7 years ago? All they said was it came from ohio.<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000037||The Fieromaster||07-09-2001||10:09 AM||||Fishtailing... gotta love it.. but ask the 3 trannies i have nuked if THEY liked fish tailing? Hehehehe!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> 2 Diff gears went and 1 set of syncros (due to bad axle seal and loss of fluid).<BR>My one set of gears went so bad they blew into the clutch housing and the pressure plate carried the gear pieces around ANNIHALATING the inside of the bellhousing!  It was BAD!!  And the 30 or so holes in the housing and the fist size one by the speedo gear!  On one occasion after the blow up I was showing Fieromaster88 how the engine ran and I almost hit him in the face with a tranny piece when i reved it up... OOOPPSIE! Guess all the parts werent all out... sorry dude!  Funny thing was the diff pin was FINE but the one gear went Bye bye!  It was the gear on the passenger side... oh well.. Time to try an Isuzu 5 speed!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||11
